def read(i):return (Path('items')/f'{i}.md').read_text()
def save(i,s):(Path('items')/f'{i}.md').write_text(s)
def swap(s,a,b):assert a in s,a[:120];return s.replace(a,b,1)
i='def-nrqm-approximations-framework-wkb-regime-model';s=read(i);s=swap(s,r'uses\n$\kappa',r'uses\n$\kappa') if False else s;s=swap(s,r'$\kappa(\xi):=\sqrt{\lambda-W(\xi)}>0$',r'$\kappa(\xi):=\sqrt{W(\xi)-\lambda}>0$');s=swap(s,r'\,d\xi =\frac1\hbar\int_{x_{a}}^{x_{b}}\sqrt{2m(V(x)-E)}\,dx',r'\,d\xi =\frac{h}{\hbar}\int_{x_{a}}^{x_{b}}\sqrt{2m(V(x)-E)}\,dx');s=swap(s,"the equality being the lemma's clause (b)","equivalently $S/h$ is the physical action in units of $\\hbar$, by the lemma's clause (b)");save(i,s)
i='ex-nrqm-approximations-smooth-barrier-tunnelling-limits';s=read(i);s=s.replace(r'4k^{2}\kappa^{2}/(k^{2}+\kappa^{2})^{2}',r'16k^{2}\kappa^{2}/(k^{2}+\kappa^{2})^{2}');a=s.index('1.2 [Rectangular limit]');b=s.index('\n\n2.1',a);s=s[:a]+r'''1.2 [Rectangular limit] Put $A:=U^2/(4E(U-E))>0$ and $t:=\kappa a$. By [L2], $T_{\rm rect}=[1+A\sinh^2 t]^{-1}$, hence $T_{\rm rect}e^{2t}=[e^{-2t}+A\sinh^2(t)e^{-2t}]^{-1}$. At fixed $E,U$, [L3] gives the denominator limit $A/4>0$, so $T_{\rm rect}e^{2t}\to4/A=16E(U-E)/U^2$. Substituting $E=\hbar^2k^2/(2m)$ and $U-E=\hbar^2\kappa^2/(2m)$ gives $16E(U-E)/U^2=16k^2\kappa^2/(k^2+\kappa^2)^2$, as asserted in (b). [L2, L3, algebra]''' +s[b:];s=s.replace('the nonunit\nprefactor','the profile-dependent\nprefactor');save(i,s)
i='pthm-nrqm-approximations-wkb-allowed-region-error';s=read(i).replace('dimensionless potential stays strictly above the energy','dimensionless potential stays strictly below the energy');save(i,s)
i='pthm-nrqm-approximations-turning-point-connection';s=read(i);s=swap(s,'(not on $h$), such that:','(not on $h$), and $h_0>0$, such that for every $0<h<h_0$:');s=swap(s,'The solution with terminal data','The solution with terminal data') if False else s;s=swap(s,'the growing terminal data $(B_{h},B_{h}\')$ obey the analogous bound','the growing branch has Airy data $(B_{h},B_{h}\')$ at $\\zeta=0$ and obeys the analogous bound');a=s.index('1.2 [The two matched');b=s.index('\n\n4.1 [Scope',a)
s=s[:a]+r'''1.2 [Matched solutions and forbidden forms] By [F3], take $w_{\mathrm{dec}}$ with Airy data $(A_h,A_h')$ at the right endpoint and $w_{\mathrm{grow}}$ with Airy data $(B_h,B_h')$ at $\zeta=0$; put $u_{\mathrm{dec}}(\xi)=a(\xi)w_{\mathrm{dec}}(\zeta(\xi))$ and similarly for the growing branch. These are exact solutions by [F1]. On the forbidden side, $2\zeta^{3/2}/(3h)=\Sigma(\xi)$ and $a(\xi)=\zeta^{1/4}(W-\lambda)^{-1/4}$. Thus [F2] and the value bounds of [F3] give the forbidden forms with $C=\tfrac12\pi^{-1/2}h^{1/6}$ and $C'=\pi^{-1/2}h^{1/6}$; the relative forbidden errors are bounded by a constant times $\varepsilon(h)+h/|\zeta|^{3/2}$ on the stated matching sections. These constants are nonzero for each $h>0$, while the error constants depend only on the fixed data. [F1, F2, F3, algebra]

1.3 [Independence for sufficiently small h] At $\zeta=0$, [F3] gives $w_{\mathrm{dec}}-A_h=O(\varepsilon(h))$ and $w_{\mathrm{dec}}'-A_h'=O(h^{-2/3}\varepsilon(h))$, since $e_h(0)=1$ and $d_h(0)=h^{-2/3}$ and $e^{\varepsilon(h)}-1=O(\varepsilon(h))$. The growing data there are exactly $B_h(0),B_h'(0)$, with $B_h(0)=O(1)$ and $B_h'(0)=O(h^{-2/3})$ by [F2]. Consequently their Wronskian at zero is $h^{-2/3}[\pi^{-1}+O(\varepsilon(h))]$, nonzero when $h$ is sufficiently small because $\varepsilon(h)\le C_1h$. Its derivative is zero for the common equation $w''=(\zeta/h^2+R)w$, so it is nonzero throughout. The invertible Liouville transformation preserves independence. Choose $h_0$ small enough for this and the supplied estimates. [F1, F2, F3, step 1.2, algebra]

2.1 [Allowed forms with additive errors] For $\xi<\xi_0$, $2|\zeta|^{3/2}/(3h)=\theta(\xi)$ and $a(\xi)=|\zeta|^{1/4}(\lambda-W)^{-1/4}$. The Airy formulas of [F2] therefore give $aA_h=2C(\lambda-W)^{-1/4}[\sin(\theta+\pi/4)+O(h/|\zeta|^{3/2})]$ and $aB_h=C'(\lambda-W)^{-1/4}[\cos(\theta+\pi/4)+O(h/|\zeta|^{3/2})]$. Adding the envelope-controlled differences of [F3] yields exactly the additive errors $\delta_{\rm a},\delta_{\rm a}'$ of (a),(b), including at sine or cosine zeros. If needed [F4] transports the data across any further fixed allowed matching section and adds its controlled error. The amplitudes are $2C$ and $C'$; no relative error at an oscillatory zero is asserted. [step 1.2, F1, F2, F3, F4, algebra]

3.1 [Derivative bounds] For either branch write $w_0=A_h$ or $B_h$ and use its respective value and derivative envelopes $e_h^{(0)},d_h^{(0)}$. The chain rule gives $u'-(a\,w_0\circ\zeta)'=a'(w-w_0)\circ\zeta+a\zeta'(w'-w_0')\circ\zeta$. Hence [F3] bounds its modulus by $C[|a'|e_h^{(0)}(\zeta)+|a|\zeta'd_h^{(0)}(\zeta)](e^{\varepsilon(h)}-1)$. The fixed-interval coefficients $a,a',\zeta'$ are bounded by [F1], and $e_h^{(0)}\le d_h^{(0)}$ for $h\le1$; the corresponding Airy derivative asymptotics of [F2] thus give the stated slope control with the derivative envelope and the matching error $h/|\zeta|^{3/2}$. No derivative of an unspecified error term is taken. [step 1.2, step 2.1, F1, F2, F3, algebra]''' +s[b:];save(i,s)
i='pthm-nrqm-approximations-nondegenerate-perturbation-expansion';s=read(i);s=swap(s,r'v=\|V\|>0$',r'v=\|V\|\ge0$');s=swap(s,'be the reduced inverse of the model clause (c)(iii), and put','be the reduced inverse of the model clause (c)(iii). In the branch $v>0$ put');s=swap(s,'Then for every real $\\lambda$ with $|\\lambda|<R$:','Then clauses (a)-(e) hold for every real $\\lambda$ with $|\\lambda|<R$\nin this positive-norm branch; clause (f) covers $v=0$ independently of $R$:');save(i,s)
i='pthm-nrqm-approximations-degenerate-first-order-splitting';s=read(i);s=swap(s,'(c) every real eigenvalue $z$ of $H(\\lambda)$ with eigenvector $\\psi\\ne0$\nlies within the first-order shift set:','(c) every real eigenvalue $z$ of $H(\\lambda)$ with eigenvector $\\psi\\ne0$\nand $|z-E|+|\\lambda|v\\le g/2$ lies within the first-order shift set:');s=s.replace('all within $\\lambda v$ of $E$','all within $|\\lambda|v$ of $E$').replace('the perturbed labels of the family\nare localised','the perturbed labels in the window of (c)\nare localised').replace('for every eigenvalue $z$;','for every eigenvalue $z$ in that window;').replace('[E-\\lambda v,E+\\lambda v]','[E-|\\lambda|v,E+|\\lambda|v]').replace('steps 1.1-3.1','steps 1.1-2.2');s=swap(s,'localisation of every perturbed eigenvalue within','localisation of every perturbed eigenvalue in the controlled gap window within');save(i,s)
i='pthm-nrqm-approximations-variational-bounds-and-min-max';s=read(i);a=s.index('3.1 [Clause (d)]');b=s.index('\n\n4.1',a);s=s[:a]+r'''3.1 [Clause (d)] Let $L\subseteq Q(H)$ have dimension $n$ and finite supremum $s=\sup\{q_H[u]:u\in L,\|u\|=1\}$. This particular $L$ belongs to the first min-max infimum of step 1.3, so $E_n\le s$ directly; attainment of the inner supremum is unnecessary. If $n=1$ and $u$ is any unit spanning vector, the unit vectors of the complex line are $\alpha u$ with $|\alpha|=1$, and the quadratic form satisfies $q_H[\alpha u]=|\alpha|^2q_H[u]=q_H[u]$. Thus $s=q_H[u]$ and $E_1=E_0$ reduces the assertion to (a). [step 1.3, step 2.1, F2, algebra]''' +s[b:];save(i,s)
i='ex-nrqm-approximations-zeeman-multiplet-splitting';s=read(i);s=s.replace('letting $g$ decrease to any positive value and\ncomparing with the exact spectrum of (b) shows the true distance is $0$','comparing with the exact spectrum of (b) shows the true distance is $0$').replace('frequency $\\gamma B_{z}$;','signed frequency $\\lambda\\gamma B_{z}$, equal to $\\gamma B_z$ at the physical coupling $\\lambda=1$;')
s=s.replace('all three eigenvalues of the three-dimensional space are simple.','if $\\gamma\\ne0$ these three eigenvalues of $V$ are simple, while for $\\gamma=0$ one has $V=0$.').replace('with the corresponding one-dimensional eigenspaces of $S_{3}$;','with the corresponding $S_3$ eigenlines when $\\lambda\\gamma\\ne0$; if $\\lambda\\gamma=0$ then $H(\\lambda)=\\varepsilon I$ and its sole eigenspace is all of $\\mathbb C^3$;')
a=s.index('3.1 [The degenerate localisation check]');b=s.index('\n\n4.1',a);s=s[:a]+r'''3.1 [The localisation check and zero branch] Since $\sigma(H_0)=\{\varepsilon\}$, any $g>0$ is a gap in the stated convention. Each eigenvalue of step 2.1 has $|z-\varepsilon|\le|\lambda|v$, so $|\lambda|v<g/4$ implies $|z-\varepsilon|+|\lambda|v<g/2$, exactly the controlled window required by [L3]. For $v>0$ the theorem therefore applies; the actual distance is already zero by the exact spectrum of step 2.1, for every real $\lambda$. One could also send $g\to\infty$ while keeping $\lambda$ fixed to make the upper bound tend to zero; decreasing $g$ would not do so. If $v=0$, then $\gamma=0$ and the family is constant, with the same zero distance directly and no division by $v$. This proves (c) in all branches. [L3, step 1.1, step 2.1, given, algebra]''' +s[b:]
s=s.replace('the transverse spin means precess at $\\gamma B_{z}$;','the transverse spin means precess at signed frequency $\\lambda\\gamma B_z$, by applying [L2] to the effective field $\\lambda\\mathbf B$; the scalar $\\varepsilon I$ contributes only a common phase and cancels from observable expectations;');save(i,s)
